  "reason": "Evidence: RNA encoder choice showed the largest effect so far — pca_n2000 (config_001, acc=0.527) substantially outperformed scgpt (config_043, acc=0.427) in an otherwise identical multimodal/resnet50/concat/singleprofile setup. Image alone is weak (0.208), confirming RNA dominates. Uncertainty: we have not yet tested scvi_n200, the third available RNA encoder, so we cannot yet rank all encoder options or determine whether the pca_n2000 advantage is general or specific. This experiment (config_028: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) is a clean single-variable swap against config_001, isolating the RNA encoder effect. It is the best use of the next budget slot because resolving the RNA encoder question (pca vs scgpt vs scvi) is the highest-leverage design decision identified so far; the result will constrain or open up many downstream experiments involving multiprofile, alternative image encoders, and fusion strategies."
}

